Info




Once Narin has full Ice, she can expend 
25
 
 
Energy
 to enter a sword dance. During the sword dance, Narin steadily drains Ice over 
 
20
 seconds, and the ability will end once she has no more Ice.

Each slash fired at an unmarked target costs 
2%
 Ice on top of the drain; slashes at marked targets cost nothing. Neither the drain nor the slash cost is affected by 
 
Ability Efficiency
; 
 
Ability Duration
 only slows the drain.


Sword dance duration = 20 s × 
 × (1 − 0.02 × unmarked slashes); a full Ice bar holds at most 50 unmarked slashes.


Ice is displayed as a light-blue orb carried by a crane, placed above the ability icons. When fully charged, a low humming sound will play and the orb will begin to shimmer.


Narin cannot gain Ice during the sword dance (including via 
 
Hakchum
).


During the sword dance, Narin projects a frost aura within 
 
6 / 7 / 7 / 8
 meter radius around her, inflicting 
 
200 / 300 / 400 / 500
 
 
Cold
 damage and 
2
 
 
Cold
 status effects per second.

This radius can gain elemental damage from 
 
Nourish
, allowing it to inflict 
 
Viral
 Status Effects.


The ice field does not require 
line of sight
.


Press the fire button (default 
LMB
 ) to launch an icy slash. Each slash hit removes 
2% / 3% / 4% / 5%
 of the enemy's 
 
Shield
s and 
base
 
 
Armor
 per 
 
Cold
 status effect on that enemy, 
before
 dealing its damage; the reduction is cumulative across hits. The slash then inflicts 
 
12,500 / 15,000 / 17,500 / 20,000
 
 
Cold
 damage with a guaranteed 
 
Cold
 status effect to every enemy in its path. If an enemy is frozen (10 
 
Cold
 Status Effects) when hit, it takes the slash damage 
twice
 and explodes to inflict 
 
6,250 / 7,500 / 8,750 / 10,000
 
 
Cold
 damage in a 
 
7 / 8 / 9 / 10
 meter radius, hitting itself and every enemy in range, with no 
Damage Falloff
.

Explosions also remove 
 
Armor
 from the enemies they hit, using each enemy's own 
 
Cold
 status effects.


The reduction also works on Overguarded enemies, using their (at most 4) 
 
Cold
 status effects; Overguarded enemies cannot be frozen until their Overguard breaks.


Slashes travel 
60
 meters, 
punching through
 terrain and enemies.


The frozen AoE explosion requires line of sight from Narin.


Enemies capped at 4 stacks of status (such as bosses or enemies with 
 
Overguard
) cannot be fully frozen, so they take neither the doubled slash damage nor cause an explosion.


Immediately on cast and every 
0.667
 seconds during the sword dance, 
1
 enemy within 
50
 meters and line of sight of Narin will be marked by a targeting ring for 
3
 seconds. Firing a slash at a marked enemy costs 
0%
 Ice, and the slash deals 
2x
 damage to every enemy it passes through, marked or not, and to the explosions it causes. A slash fired at an unmarked enemy deals 1x damage, even to marked enemies in its path.

When the crosshair is aiming at a targeted enemy, it will turn blue, and the enemy's targeting ring will spin.


Line of sight is only required for the enemy to be targeted with a ring. A slash can be fired if the crosshair is aimed at a target that is no longer in line of sight.


Marks are prioritized on enemies close to the targeting reticle.


While Nurinarim is active, Narin can only move, jump, roll and cast 
 
Hakchum
 and 
Transference
.

Narin becomes translucent when rolling and jumping, though this is only a visual effect.


Narin has limited influence over her aerial momentum during Nurinarim.


Narin's ground speed during the sword dance is the same as her 
sprinting
 speed.


The roll is affected by 
Parkour Velocity
 and 
Dodge Speed
 via 
 
Amalgam Barrel Diffusion
.


Nullifier
 bubbles do not end the sword dance, but Narin cannot fire slashes while inside a bubble. Enemies inside a bubble cannot be marked and take no damage from slashes aimed at them; a slash aimed at a marked enemy outside or behind the bubble works normally.


Recasting Nurinarim ends the sword dance, retaining the Ice that was not spent while it was active.






Kit Interactions




Nurinarim requires full Ice to cast. Ice is generated by her other 3 abilities:

Casts of 
 
Neote
 that hit an enemy grant 
7%
 Ice, plus an additional 
0.5%
 Ice per hit.


 
Naraemagi
 generates 
5%
 Ice for on cast, plus an additional 
1%
 Ice for each enemy hit by the ability.


Each enemy hit by 
 
Hakchum's
 initial cast generates 
1%
 Ice.


 
Hakchum
's 
 
Cold
 
Damage Vulnerability
 and Sangodae's ×1.25 ability bonus multiply each other.


 
Naraemagi
 absorbing 
 
Cold
 status effects from a frozen enemy unfreezes it immediately, so it will not explode until refrozen.






